// Two literal bounds counting down. Both values are in hand at compile time, a range only
// counts up, so this program says one thing and would do another — refused.
//
// The asymmetry is deliberate and is in tests/pass/for_range.bx: `for i in a..b` with `a > b`
// at RUNTIME runs zero times, because the lowering is `i = a; while i < b`, and because
// `for i in 0..len(xs)` over an empty array is correct code that must not trap. A compiler
// refuses what it can SEE; a range it cannot see is not an error.
for i in 3..0 {
    print(i);
}
